# UnitConfig Schema (Draft v1)

This document fixes the canonical structure for our unified unit configuration snapshot (`UnitConfig`).  
It mirrors the dataclasses in `pipeline/config/unit_config.py` and is designed to be a superset of the data
we import from Wialon `.wlp` exports. The same schema will be used when we populate objects from other
telemetry providers, so every section keeps flexible `extra`/`meta` blocks for vendor-specific fields.
For machine validation the JSON schema is also stored as `pipeline/config/unit_config.schema.json`.

## Sections

| Section | Dataclass | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `general` | `GeneralConfig` | Identity: name, UID/IMEI, phones, password/pins, hardware tag |
| `icon` | `IconConfig` | Marker/icon metadata for UI |
| `hw_config` | `HWConfig` + `HWParam` | Tracker configuration parameters and flags |
| `sensors[]` | `SensorConfig` | Unified sensor definitions (type, formulas, validation, calibration) |
| `sensors[].calibration` | `SensorCalibration` + `CalibrationPoint`/`CalibrationSegment` | Piecewise-linear conversion tables and XY points |
| `sensors[].validation` | `SensorValidation` | Value filters (min/max, hysteresis, quality flags) |
| `counters` | `CounterConfig` | Runtime counters (mileage, engine hours, total fuel) |
| `profile[]` | `ProfileField` | Custom attributes defined by operator |
| `intervals[]` | `IntervalConfig` | Notification/collection interval presets |
| `report_props` | `Dict[str, Any]` | Defaults for analytics/reports |
| `aliases[]` | `Dict[str, Any]` | Localized names/tags |
| `driving`, `trip` | `Dict[str, Any]` | Trip detection and driver behaviour presets |
| `advanced` | `Dict[str, Any]` | Advanced options (primary sensors, styles, etc.) |
| `extra` | `Dict[str, Any]` | Future-proof storage for any unknown section |

### Sensor calibration detail

Each sensor may have both raw XY points (exactly as entered by the operator) and the derived linear
segments used for fast calculation (`Y = a * X + b`). `segments[].start_x` marks the beginning of a
piecewise range. Tanks or complex sensors can be distinguished via `tank_id`. When importing Wialon
tables we store both representations so they can be exported back without loss.

### Validation and expressions

`SensorConfig.parameters` contains the source formulas/expression tree (e.g. `p1`, `p2`, `flags`,
bit masks). `expression` is a normalized textual form we can evaluate locally. `SensorValidation`
stores the policy chosen in UI (`mode`, bounds, hysteresis) plus `params` for type-specific options.

## JSON Schema

The following JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) formalizes the structure. Optional objects may be omitted
or set to `null`; arrays default to empty.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://cfbot.local/schemas/unit_config.json",
  "title": "UnitConfig",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["unit_id", "source_kind"],
  "properties": {
    "unit_id": {"type": "integer"},
    "source_kind": {"type": "string"},
    "dump_ts": {"type": "integer"},
    "general": {"$ref": "#/$defs/GeneralConfig"},
    "icon": {"$ref": "#/$defs/IconConfig"},
    "hw_config": {"$ref": "#/$defs/HWConfig"},
    "counters": {"$ref": "#/$defs/CounterConfig"},
    "advanced": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}},
    "profile": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/ProfileField"}
    },
    "intervals": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/IntervalConfig"}
    },
    "sensors": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/SensorConfig"}
    },
    "report_props": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}},
    "aliases": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
    },
    "driving": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}},
    "trip": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}},
    "extra": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
  },
  "$defs": {
    "GeneralConfig": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["name"],
      "properties": {
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "uid": {"type": "string"},
        "uid2": {"type": "string"},
        "phone": {"type": "string"},
        "phone2": {"type": "string"},
        "password": {"type": "string"},
        "hardware": {"type": "string"},
        "extra": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "IconConfig": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "library": {"type": "string"},
        "url": {"type": "string"},
        "rotation_mode": {"type": "string"},
        "extra": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "HWConfig": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "hardware": {"type": "string"},
        "full_data": {"type": "boolean"},
        "params": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/HWParam"}
        },
        "extra": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "HWParam": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["name"],
      "properties": {
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "label": {"type": "string"},
        "type": {"type": "string"},
        "value": {},
        "default": {},
        "description": {"type": "string"},
        "readonly": {"type": "boolean"},
        "minval": {"type": "number"},
        "maxval": {"type": "number"},
        "extra": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "CounterConfig": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "values": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {"type": "number"}}
      }
    },
    "ProfileField": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["field_id", "name", "value"],
      "properties": {
        "field_id": {"type": "integer"},
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "value": {},
        "meta": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "IntervalConfig": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["interval_id", "name"],
      "properties": {
        "interval_id": {"type": "integer"},
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "params": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "SensorConfig": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["sensor_id", "name", "type"],
      "properties": {
        "sensor_id": {"type": "integer"},
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "type": {"type": "string"},
        "units": {"type": "string"},
        "description": {"type": "string"},
        "parameters": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}},
        "expression": {"type": "string"},
        "validation": {"$ref": "#/$defs/SensorValidation"},
        "calibration": {"$ref": "#/$defs/SensorCalibration"},
        "meta": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "SensorValidation": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "mode": {"type": "string"},
        "min_value": {"type": "number"},
        "max_value": {"type": "number"},
        "hysteresis": {"type": "number"},
        "params": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "SensorCalibration": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["sensor_id"],
      "properties": {
        "sensor_id": {"type": "integer"},
        "tank_id": {"type": "string"},
        "points": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/CalibrationPoint"}
        },
        "segments": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/CalibrationSegment"}
        },
        "smoothing": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}},
        "source": {"type": "string"},
        "updated_at": {"type": "integer"},
        "meta": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}}
      }
    },
    "CalibrationPoint": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["raw", "value"],
      "properties": {
        "raw": {"type": "number"},
        "value": {"type": "number"}
      }
    },
    "CalibrationSegment": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["start_x", "a", "b"],
      "properties": {
        "start_x": {"type": "number"},
        "a": {"type": "number"},
        "b": {"type": "number"}
      }
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

## Notes / Next Steps

1. When new providers expose extra fields we extend dataclasses, update this schema, and bump the `$id` version.
2. For persistence, configs are saved as JSON documents validated against the schema; binary exports (e.g. `.wlp`)
   rely on adapters that map between vendor keys and our canonical names.
3. Calibration editors should work on `points` and regenerate `segments` automatically to keep X a b consistent.

This doc completes Step 1 of the plan (formal description of UnitConfig). Later steps will wire a config service,
import/export pipelines, and UI/editor features on top of the same schema.

## Importing Wialon `.wlp`

Use `pipeline/adapters/wialon_wlp_import.py` (or the CLI `python -m pipeline.cli.import_wlp --unit-id ...`) to convert a Wialon
`.wlp` export into `UnitConfig`. The importer maps `general`, `icon`, `hwConfig`, `sensors`, `counters`, `advProps`, `profile`,
`intervals`, and other sections directly into the dataclasses described above, preserving unknown fields inside the `extra` maps.
